## 15. Resolved Decisions

| Question | Decision |
|---|---|
| **Vault sync** | User's responsibility. Pulse reads/writes local files. Recommended: Self-hosted LiveSync (CouchDB) or Syncthing. |
| **LLM cost management** | Not in MVP. Can be added later. |
| **Multi-user support** | Single user only. No user scoping in the schema. |
| **Email content depth** | Default ingestion: subject + sender + timestamp. Full email body is accessible to the model on demand for deeper analysis. |
| **Project name** | Pulse |
| **Deployment target** | Any always-on machine. No Kubernetes or Docker required. Single Python process is the default. |
| **Notification channel (dev)** | Telegram bot. |
| **Notification channel (prod)** | Companion app push notifications. |
| **LLM providers** | Claude API and OpenAI API, with an abstract interface to support local models (Ollama) later. |
| **Companion app networking** | User handles reachability via VPN (Tailscale/Netbird recommended), Cloudflare Tunnel, or local network. Pulse binds to a local address; networking is not the project's concern. |
| **Mobile browsing capture** | Not in scope. Desktop Chrome extension covers browsing for now. |
| **Google API rate limits** | All planned pull frequencies are well within free-tier quotas. Gmail allows 15,000 quota units/user/min (we use ~1,500/day). Calendar allows 1M requests/day (we use ~96). YouTube allows 10,000 units/day (we use ~240). No issue. |
| **iOS geofence limit** | 20 regions is sufficient for MVP. Rotation strategy deferred to post-MVP. |
| **Offline resilience** | Host machine is assumed always-on. Companion app buffers events locally and pushes on next successful connection. |

## 16. What's Next

With all major design questions resolved, the next step is implementation. Recommended build order:

1. **Scaffold the project** -- Python package structure, config system, SQLite schema, vault directory setup.
2. **Build the event store and connector interface** -- Get the abstract `DataConnector` and `Event` classes working with SQLite persistence.
3. **Google Calendar connector** -- Simplest API, immediate utility. OAuth2 flow here unlocks Gmail and YouTube later.
4. **Gmail connector** -- High-value data source, reuses the same OAuth2 token.
5. **Daily digest summarizer** -- First LLM integration. Reads from event store, writes markdown to vault.
6. **Telegram bot** -- Notification delivery + correction handling. Closes the feedback loop.
7. **Companion app (Flutter, iOS)** -- Location tracking + webhook push. Geofence management.
8. **Insight generator** -- The hard part. Pattern detection, cross-source correlation, weekly/monthly reviews.
